            <h2>Types of Campaigns Available</h2>
            
            <h3><a href="/local-seo">Geographic Visibility</a></h3>
            <p>For businesses that serve customers in specific areas. Includes Google Business Profile work, citations, review management, and location-based content. Essential for retail, hospitality, health, trades and any business where customers search with location intent.</p>
            
            <h3><a href="/seo-audit">One-Off Audits</a></h3>
            <p>Technical and content audits that identify what's holding your site back. You get a prioritised list of issues and recommendations. Some businesses use this as a starting point then implement fixes themselves. Others have me implement the fixes as part of ongoing work.</p>
            
            <h3><a href="/keyword-research">Phrase Research</a></h3>
            <p>Understanding what your potential customers actually type into Google. Not just obvious terms but the long-tail queries that often convert better. I use a mix of tools and manual analysis to find opportunities your competitors are missing.</p>
            
            <h3><a href="/technical-seo-services">Technical Work</a></h3>
            <p>Site speed, mobile performance, crawl efficiency, schema markup, and fixing technical issues that prevent ranking. Technical work is often the quickest win for sites that have good content but poor performance.</p>
            
            <h3><a href="/ecommerce-seo-sydney">Online Store Campaigns</a></h3>
            <p>Product page improvements, category structure, faceted navigation handling, and schema for products and reviews. Online stores have specific requirements around duplicate content, pagination and product feeds.</p>
